{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:2136b702e946f630","name":"Disabling the Tracking Device","source":{"id":"source:reference-2136b702e946f630","title":"Disabling the Tracking Device","revision":21167,"timestamp":"2024-08-26T01:17:09Z","sha256":"5dcae9645c34d94cc9965c0630a881e3e913319a9b70755fda229235bfc36f13","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=21167","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Disabling%20the%20Tracking%20Device&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-2136b702e946f630","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Galaxy of Intrigue"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Galaxy_of_Intrigue"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["As the heroes leave the Duro System, they might breathe a sigh of relief, or they might search their ship to see if the Imperials have hidden a tracking device on board. If the heroes locate the tracking device near the ship's engines, they can attempt to disable it. However, they realize that the device is rigged with ",{"tag":"a","children":["Explosive Charges"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Explosive_Charges"}," that could detonate if they try to remove or deactivate it. A DC 18 ",{"tag":"a","children":["Knowledge (Technology)"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Knowledge_(Technology)"}," check reveals that such an explosion at this location could destroy a significant portion of the ship- perhaps the whole vessel.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Disabling the Tracking Device Statistics (CL 9)"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Complexity:"]}," 2 (8 Successes before 3 Failures)\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Suggested ",{"tag":"a","children":["Skills"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Skills","referenceId":"reference:66d0f523a379b2de"},":"]}," The following are suggested Primary Skills for this ",{"tag":"a","children":["Skill Challenge"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Skill_Challenge"},":\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"ul","children":[{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Mechanics"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Mechanics","referenceId":"reference:1c74a0e2ceaaeb28"}," (DC 30):"]}," The heroes use the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Disable Device"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Disable_Device"}," application of the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Mechanics"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Mechanics","referenceId":"reference:1c74a0e2ceaaeb28"}," skill (which requires a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Security Kit"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Security_Kit","referenceId":"reference:b3de8e74a439451f"},") and manage to disable part of it."]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Knowledge (Technology)"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Knowledge_(Technology)"}," (DC 28):"]}," The heroes recall whatever information they know about the proper way to disable tracking devices or explosives."]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Use the Force"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Use_the_Force","referenceId":"reference:74883d1dd46b87fe"}," (DC 28):"]}," The heroes use the ship's computer to try to link to the tracking device and slice into its programming."]}]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Challenge Effects"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["The following is a suggested ",{"tag":"a","children":["Challenge Effect"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Challenge_Effect"}," for this Skill Challenge:\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"ul","children":[{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Catastrophic Failure"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Catastrophic_Failure","referenceId":"reference:8e66c70d3771541a"},":"]}," Disarming the rigged device is a delicate task with dire consequences. Any hero who fails a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Skill Check"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Skill_Check"}," by 10 or more accrues two Failures instead of one."]}]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Success and Failure"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Success:"]}," The heroes fully disarm the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Explosives"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Explosives"}," and disable the tracking device.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Failure:"]}," The heroes cannot remove the demolitions safely. Roll a d20 and add the total number of Successes earned during the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Skill Challenge"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Skill_Challenge"},". If the result equals or exceeds 15, the heroes are unable to disarm the device, but it does not explode. If the result does not meet or beat DC 15, the device explodes, dealing 10d6 points of damage to the ship's engine room.\n"]},"\n","\n","\n","\n\n","\n\n","\n"]}}
